class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Why hydration monitoring matters</h2></div><div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><p>Water intake is one of the most clinically informative measurements in small animal medicine, and almost no household tracks it. Increased drinking is a leading early indicator of chronic kidney disease, diabetes and hyperadrenocorticism.</p><p>Hydration Monitoring measures consumption to the millilitre per animal and compares it against weight-adjusted expected ranges.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Capabilities</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">What this includes</h2></div><ul class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Millilitre-level measurement</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Fountain-integrated volumetric tracking, not estimation.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Per-animal attribution</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Individual identification at shared water sources.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Polydipsia alerting</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Sustained intake above weight-adjusted thresholds escalated for veterinary review.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Dehydration warnings</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Reduced intake correlated with heat, activity and illness markers.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Water quality management</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Filter life and circulation monitoring to keep water appealing.</p></div></li></ul></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center"><div><p class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Outcomes</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">What owners typically see</h2><ul class="mt-8 space-y-4"><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Renal and endocrine disease indicators surfaced early.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Objective intake figures to bring to a veterinary consultation.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Improved drinking in cats, which are chronically under-hydrated.</li></ul></div><img alt="PawlogicTech hardware used for hydration monitoring" class="w-full rounded-3xl object-cover shadow-lift" decoding="async" height="900" loading="lazy" src="<?php echo esc_url( get_template_directory_uri() ); ?>/assets/images/tech-sensor.webp" width="1200"/></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>FAQ</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Hydration Monitoring questions</h2></div><div class="divide-y divide-border rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card"><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">What counts as excessive drinking?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Broadly, sustained intake above roughly 100ml per kilogram of bodyweight per day warrants veterinary investigation, though the alert threshold is tuned to your animal's own established baseline.</p></details><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">Does evaporation distort the readings?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">No. Evaporation is modelled from ambient temperature and humidity and subtracted from the intake figure.</p></details></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] t